WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:04.840
[ groans ]

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:06.320
Let's do this.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.260
Good morning, John!

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.200
First, thank you so much
for your video on Tuesday.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.400
Now, of course we both recognize
that we never want this channel

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.440
to become like a current evens
and politics channel,

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.820
but I also think that you are very, very 
good at making that type of video.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.100
And I came away from watching it
being like "Oh, I get things better."

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.880
Sometimes, I think that when we talk
about politics here on Vlogbrothers,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.280
that we are just making it worse.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.100
Just deepening the echo chamber.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.940
That by spouting my liberal viewpoints,

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.020
I'm chasing off everybody
that might disagree with me,

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.560
and ending all opportunity for discourse.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.220
But look. I am me.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.240
I have my values, and I have my worldview,

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.560
and I believe things.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.980
Like global warming is caused by people,

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.160
and it will be one of the biggest challenges
humanity will ever face together.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:53.740
And it's ludicrous that we spent
so much time denying

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.100
the joy of marriage to people

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.620
just because of the people
they happened to love.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.820
And just like I think the government
shouldn't have spent all those years

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.620
discriminating against people
because of their sexual orientation,

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.100
I don't think that it should be
legal for businesses to do that.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:12.020
And creating and feeding an irrational fear of
people who want to come to America,

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.220
just like my ancestors wanted to
come to America because they believed

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.400
in the same dream that we all believe in,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.700
I think that it's an effective, but 
dangerous way to gain power.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.460
I believe that these things are true
and that running the country

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.040
while denying them is a bad idea.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.900
Do I want to drive away the
people who disagree with me?

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.260
No, but that doesn't mean I am not
gonna say the things that I believe.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.520
I am me, and I am here to be all
the parts of me that I want to be.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.940
I'm here to be silly,
I'm here to be thoughtful,

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:41.680
and I'm here to use the platform that I have
to fight for the things that I believe in.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.780
Not every day, but some days.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.980
I'm not here to insult the people
who disagree with me

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.240
because, like, I want them
to watch this more than anyone,

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.620
but when I see things I believe in,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.800
like human rights and objectivity

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.980
and liberal democracy being threatened,

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.500
I'm not gonna not talk about that.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.000
Last weekend, I went on Twitter and I
offered to donate $5 to the ACLU

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.380
for every person who submitted to me a
hand-drawn message of support

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:09.980
for immigrants and refugees.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.640
I got over 2,000 submissions,

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.380
and some of them were just
way above and beyond.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.160
Just beautiful pieces of art.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.040
This weekend only from now until 
midnight on Sunday,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.720
Some time zone. I'm not sure which.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.620
The artists of some of those works are
selling them as posters at dftba.com.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:30.880
As part of President Trump's ban on 
all refugees entering the United States,

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.520
federal funding to local organizations that
help refugees find work and get training

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:39.260
and have access to simple things
that they don't have

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.800
when they arrive in America
because they have nothing

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.480
like toothpaste and tampons.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.000
Has been eliminated.
It just doesn't exist anymore.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.080
And those organizations now
are not in a great place.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.600
So not only have we stopped helping
people who want to come here,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.080
we've stopped helping people
who are already here.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.680
That doesn't seem like a good idea.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.880
So 100% of the proceeds
from the sale of these posters

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:01.820
is going to be divided up among
a bunch of different organizations

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.580
that do that very important
and very good work.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.060
Because, look, we can make a difference,

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.520
and we can work for the
world that we want to see.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.640
That isn't creating an echo chamber.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.560
That's creating change.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.320
John, I will see you on Tuesday.

